From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IamMaxim <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 22:42:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] strip: remove cloud-coupled LLM provider modules

Removes the language_models provider modules for cloud-coupled LLM
backends: anthropic, bedrock, cloud (zed-hosted), deepseek, google,
mistral, open_ai, open_router, opencode, openai_subscribed,
vercel_ai_gateway, x_ai. The provider registrations in
language_models::init are gone; only the local-first OpenAI-compatible,
Ollama, and LM Studio providers are registered.

Settings: AllLanguageModelSettings shrinks to only what those three
backends need; the per-provider sub-settings come from the same
SettingsContent fields, which are left intact (other crates still
read them) but are otherwise unused.

The standalone protocol crates (anthropic, bedrock, deepseek,
google_ai, mistral, open_ai, open_router, opencode, x_ai,
edit_prediction_cli, language_models_cloud) are kept on disk for now:
they remain referenced as type libraries (open_ai::Response by
edit_prediction, google_ai::GoogleModelMode by agent_servers, etc.).
They will be torn out fully in the client/zed_llm_client strip.

The language_models::provider::anthropic::telemetry module is kept,
but its report functions are gutted to no-ops so the inline assistant
/ buffer codegen / terminal codegen call sites continue to compile
while no telemetry is sent.

open_ai_compatible.rs now imports the OpenAi event mappers directly
from the open_ai crate (previously it re-exported them via the now
deleted provider/open_ai.rs).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
